[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'At SEMA 2025, we introduced something that had never been sold to the general public before. Infrared lighting that we created exclusively for military users. Today it is finally available to you. This is a complete line. The SS3 IR module for'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'illuminating the road ahead, the compact and flexible C1 IR module, the combined C1 Dual module with visible and infrared light on one mount, and the "follow me" light for moving in'

[00:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a group at night. Each is available with a wavelength of 850 or 940 nanometers, operates from 9 to 16 volts, has high and low power modes, is fully regulated'

[00:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: ', is made in the USA, and is tested in real military conditions. Plus, it\'s covered by our limited lifetime warranty. One note about safety, and it\'s important. Although you cannot'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'see this light clearly, it is still real radiation. Do not look directly at any of these lights . It can still damage your eyes. All of our Stage series IR lenses are designed and manufactured'

[01:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in-house. You will notice that each of them has a black lens instead of a clear one. This is not tinting, it is a material that only transmits the IR spectrum. We build our optics with thicker walls than usual, which'

[01:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'blocks more visible red light than other counterparts on the market. You can choose between two wavelengths: 850 or 940 nanometers. It\'s not about brightness or dimness. This'

[01:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'depends on what range your night vision equipment is set to. One last thing: you won\'t hear us talking about lumens on this product. This is the visible light scale and it does not apply here. Instead, we'

[01:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'use measures of radiant intensity and radiation. Different scale, different tools—this is how IR products should be measured in general. Okay, let\'s move on to the line review. First, the SS3 IR module is'

[01:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your main light for moving forward. Available in 850 or 940 nanometer options, with Sport or Pro power levels and combined optics to provide width'

[02:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and range at the same time. High and low power, full brightness adjustment. If you need serious IR range , this is the one for you . Next is the C1 IR module. Same technology, smaller'

[02:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'size for extra light where it\'s needed, with a choice of narrow, wide or flood optics. Great for custom builds or compact and flexible mounting options. Then—the C1 Dual model. Two'

[02:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'modules, one housing. Infrared light on one side, visible white light with red backlight on the other, on one common mount. This is designed to switch between visible light and'

[02:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'night vision without using two separate systems. And lastly, the " follow me" flashlight. This device is designed to be visible, not hidden. It creates a clear three- dot pattern that is clearly visible through'

[02:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'night vision devices, so vehicles behind can keep their distance in the dark. Available individually or in pairs, 850 or 940, has an IP67 protection rating. If you are riding in a group at night,'

[03:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this will help everyone stay together. So , that\'s the whole line. SS3 for IR range ahead, C1 for compact and flexible installation, dual unit when you need visible and IR light on'

[03:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one mount, and " follow me" to keep the group together at night. Whatever you use IR for: hunting, site work, security and surveillance, or just moving around in a group'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
